title: Benchmark Infrastructure

files:
  - em.prog:em.benchmark.coremark/BenchAlgI.em.ts
  - em.prog:em.benchmark.coremark/CoreBench.em.ts
  - em.prog:em.benchmark.coremark/Crc.em.ts
  - em.prog:em.benchmark.coremark/Utils.em.ts
  - .assets/img-102-02-01.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]Benchmark Infrastructure}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * tour scope
      * shared support layer
      * CoreBench as benchmark engine
      * algorithms come next

  - cmds:
      - close 5
      - open 1
    focus: [1, 1]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |
      {[ht,$look]%[cu]BenchAlgI% &ndash; quick peek}

      The {[cu]BenchAlgI} interfaces defines a common set of func&shy;tions implemented by all benchmark algorithm modules:

      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} {[cu]CoreBench}&nbsp; [examined in this tour]<br>
      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} {[cu]ListBench},{[cu]MatrixBench},{[cu]StateBench}&nbsp; [in next tour]

      The {[cu]ActiveRunnerP} program viewed earlier illustra&shy;ted calls to {[cf]setup} and {[cf]run} via {[cu]CoreBench}.

      {[in]%[cf]kind% and %[cf]print% primarily support program debug.}

      In general, {[cu]CoreBench} will forward calls to its {[cu]BenchAlgI} functions to the other algorithm modules.

  - cmds:
      - open 2
      - mark 2 A 30
    focus: [2, 32]
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]%[cu]CoreBench% &ndash; %[cx]em$targ% details}

  - cmds:
      - open 2
    focus: [2, 1]
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]%[cu]CoreBench% &ndash; %[cx]em$meta% details}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * run path
      * workload dispatch
      * print / CRC reporting

  - cmds:
      - open 4
      - mark 4 A 13
    focus: [4, 9]
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]%[cu]Utils% &ndash; details}

      The {[cu]Utils} module exports a common set of constants, types, and accessors used by sibling **EMS** units.

      The module encapsulates two {[cs]$table} datasets {[bm,A]} which respectively hold {[ct]seed_t} constants and {[ct]sum_t} variables.

  - cmds:
      - open 3
    focus: [3, 1]
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]%[cu]Crc% &ndash; details}

  - cmds:
      - close 5
      - close 4
      - close 3
      - close 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]Extra Credit}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * inspect how each workload satisfies BenchAlgI
      * trace one CRC value from workload to final report
      * compare this infrastructure with ActiveRunnerP

  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$done]Next Steps}

      {[in]DRAFT}

      * infrastructure is now in place
      * next tour focuses on MatrixBench, StateBench, and ListBench
      * same map, different layer
